WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.730
Here's a French sentence: «Tu
aimes le sport.» You like sport.

2
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.750
To ask the question, English
needs an extra word at the front:

3
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:12.380
'Do you like sport?' French
can ask it with the same words,

4
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.890
in the same order.

5
00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.490
On paper, you just add a question mark.

6
00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.630
But out loud, nobody
can see a question mark.

7
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.220
So how can you turn 'You like sport' into

8
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:25.740
a French question without
changing a single word?

9
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.500
In this mission, you'll take
three roads to the same question.

10
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.560
Then you'll spin the question-word wheel,

11
00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:35.100
swap and bridge, and make
questions in the lab.

12
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.390
Your mission: find the trick that
turns a statement into a question.
